# Anvil Rules

## Critical: O(1) I/O on Hot Paths
All hot-path operations (claim, ack, push, stats) MUST be O(1).
Scans are only acceptable for background tasks (GC, recovery).

## Key Schema
```
meta:{queue}                     -> QueueMeta (claim_seq, push_seq, counters)
pending:{queue}:{seq}            -> msg_id
msg:{queue}:{msg_id}             -> Message JSON
claimed:{queue}:{msg_id}         -> ClaimInfo JSON
acked:{queue}:{ts}:{msg_id}      -> ""
state:{namespace}:{key}          -> value bytes
```

## Guidelines
- Use direct key access, never scan in hot paths
- Maintain counters instead of counting via scan
- Batch operations with WriteBatch for atomicity
- See `lib/anvil-rs/AGENTS.md` for full constraints
